{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-007", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Turkiye's yarn exports rise 2.6% as imports fall 16.6% in Jan–Aug", "content": "Turkiye's yarn exports rose 2.63 per cent YoY to $1.368 billion in January–August 2026, while imports fell 16.62 per cent to $1.159 billion, improving the trade balance.\nEgypt, Italy and Portugal led export destinations; China and India remained the top suppliers, according to TexPro.\nExports by volume reached 379.485 million kg, while imports stood at 499.016 million kg.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/turkiye-s-yarn-exports-rise-2-6-as-imports-fall-16-6-in-jan-aug-314361-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-008", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["fast_fashion"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rising import costs put ultra-fast fashion’s price edge at risk", "content": "Europe ended the EU €150 exemption for low-value distance-sale consignments on July 1, 2026, adding a temporary €3 duty through July 1, 2028.\nA €2 Union handling fee is due from November 1, with multi-item baskets facing charges before VAT.\nLow-value imported items reached 5.88 billion in 2025, about 4.2 times 2022, while China accounted for 91 per cent of 2024 volume.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/rising-import-costs-put-ultra-fast-fashion-s-price-edge-at-risk-314380-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-009", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Will the US-Bangladesh ART reshape raw material sourcing dynamics?", "content": "The US-Bangladesh Agreement on Reciprocal Trade could give US suppliers a stronger foothold by tying zero-tariff access for some Bangladeshi apparel exports to US-made textile inputs.\nExperts say China and India remain entrenched in Bangladesh’s supply chain, with China strong in fabrics and India in yarn.\nCost, proximity and delivery reliability may limit any major sourcing shift.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/will-the-us-bangladesh-art-reshape-raw-material-sourcing-dynamics--314327-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-010", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Luxury’s split market: Ultra-rich spend, aspirational buyers retreat", "content": "Global luxury fashion revenue fell 0.5 per cent in 2025 and is forecast to grow 2.2 per cent in 2026, with growth tapering towards 2031 as aspirational buyers curb spending.\nLVMH led luxury goods in 2025 with a 21 per cent share; fashion held 29 per cent, behind watches and jewellery at 34 per cent.\nUS 2026 revenue is estimated at $96.9 billion, ahead of China at $92.7 billion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/luxury-s-split-market-ultra-rich-spend-aspirational-buyers-retreat-314378-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-20-011", "date": "2026-10-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Bangladesh's apparel exports to EU may gain in late 2026: Eurostat", "content": "Bangladesh’s apparel exports to the EU could regain momentum late in 2026 and in 2027 as the bloc’s import decline narrows, according to the Eurostat data. \nEU apparel imports fell 3.83 per cent to €60.29 billion (~$67.74 billion) in January-August; Bangladesh’s shipments dropped 11.67 per cent to €11.93 billion (~$13.40 billion). \nAugust EU import value rose 0.72 per cent year on year.  ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-apparel-exports-to-eu-may-gain-in-late-2026-eurostat-314381-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
